B = [
('Moog Music','North America','1970s-present','instruments','In the style of Moog Music, warm, handcrafted, scientific vintage modernism. Bold black and white identity built from a wide, rounded, lowercase wordmark whose big circular letters are linked by a single continuous looping stroke, with a small slanted cut inside each round. Solid dark walnut and oiled hardwood paired with matte black and brushed silver panels, white printed labels in a clear sans-serif, and thin white lines that group areas together. Accents of orange, red and cream appear sparingly. Forms are slanted, wedge-like and sturdy with softly eased corners, exposed joinery, and a laboratory-meets-furniture honesty. Monochrome stamped badges and tidy technical diagrams in black on white.'),
('Roland','East Asia','1980s-present','instruments','In the style of Roland, crisp, technical Japanese electronics identity. A wide, heavy wordmark in custom geometric uppercase letters with doubled parallel strokes through the letters, shown in white on black, orange on white or solid blue, often paired with a small rounded-rectangle outline emblem. Palette is graphite black, charcoal grey, white and a signature orange with cobalt blue and red as secondary accents. Forms are angular, flat, wedge-profiled and slim with sharp edges, matte textured plastic and satin metal, and tidy grids of small coloured markings and fine white printed lines. Packaging uses simple flat colour fields, minimal and confident.'),
('Teenage Engineering','Europe','2010s-present','instruments','In the style of Teenage Engineering, minimalist Scandinavian-geek graphic design. The emblem is a chunky black hexagonal nut-like shape fused with a bold round form, set above a tiny, lowercase, light sans-serif wordmark with tight spacing. Everything is black on white or white on black with exact grids, thin technical outlines, small monospaced captions and numbered diagrams. Materials are anodised aluminium, matte white plastic and soft silicone in signal orange, light grey, cream and occasional pastel or neon pops. Forms are thin, flat, rectangular and precisely rounded, like clean engineering drawings made physical, playful and deadpan.'),
('Bose','North America','1980s-present','electronics','In the style of Bose, understated premium consumer design. A compact black wordmark in slanted, heavy, wide italic uppercase letters with a thin underline, set small on large calm fields of white, light grey or black. Forms are softly rounded, pebble-like and smooth with gentle tapering and seamless joins. Finishes are matte soft-touch plastic, fine woven fabric, satin aluminium and soft leather-like trim in black, soft white, silver, sand, sage, dusty blue and deep navy. Fine linear sketch-style illustrations in black on white, and sleek packaging printed with bold angled lettering and clean colour planes in teal, orange or blue. Quiet, polished and comfortable.'),
('Sonos','North America','2010s-present','electronics','In the style of Sonos, calm, matte, tactile modern minimalism. A tiny, widely letter-spaced uppercase wordmark in a thin geometric sans-serif, often debossed or printed in a single tone. Palette is soft black, pure white, warm sand, kraft brown, sage, cloud grey and dusty blue with occasional deep red or orange glow on black. Forms are smooth cuboids, cylinders and softly rounded slabs, wrapped in fine perforated metal or woven textile with no visible fasteners. Surfaces are matte and slightly grainy with crisp edges. Natural moulded-fibre and kraft paper textures and quiet monochrome layouts with ample empty space.'),
('Technics','East Asia','1970s-80s','electronics','In the style of Technics, confident Japanese audio-era branding. A bold, heavy, rounded mixed-case wordmark with a distinctive serif-like flair on the T, set in gold, silver, white or black, often on gold-edged badge plates. Palette is brushed silver, matte black, champagne gold with accents of vermilion red, orange and amber, in strong blocky colour contrast on labels and printed graphics. Finishes are thick brushed aluminium, glossy black lacquer, smoked acrylic and engraved fine scale lines. Forms are wide, flat, low and balanced with calm horizontal emphasis, precise rectangles and slim rounded corners, serious, weighty and polished.'),
('Zenith Radio','North America','1930s-50s','electronics','In the style of Zenith Radio, mid-century American promotional elegance. A sharp, angular script wordmark with a lightning-bolt Z set within a lettered banner, framed by streamlined curved panels. Palette is cream, ivory, walnut brown, warm gold, tomato red, teal and ink black on aged-paper tones. Forms are streamlined with generous rounded corners, stepped silhouettes and sunburst radiating lines, in polished figured wood veneer, glossy bakelite, chrome strips and brass trim. Vintage printed graphics use bold slab and condensed lettering, hand-inked flourishes, starburst badges and optimistic flat colour blocks with slight halftone texture.'),
('Philips','Europe','1930s-present','electronics','In the style of Philips, optimistic Dutch industrial design. The emblem is a rounded shield containing wavy parallel lines and several four-pointed stars, drawn in bold cobalt blue on white or in white on blue, with a wide, clean, uppercase sans-serif wordmark. Palette is strong electric blue, white, pale grey, with ivory, mustard, tangerine and pastel tints in older pieces and fresh cyan, navy and sunrise gold in newer ones. Forms are friendly, rounded, smooth and gently curved with glossy and soft matte plastics, bakelite, light wood and satin metal. Clear, calm, geometric graphics with generous spacing, cheerful and trustworthy.'),
('Telefunken','Europe','1930s-60s','electronics','In the style of Telefunken, bold German technical-graphics identity. A diamond-shaped emblem in black, white or red and blue, holding stacked uppercase letters in a heavy block sans-serif, with jagged lightning-like arrows radiating left and right from the sides. Printed graphics and labels use vivid orange, ultramarine, black and cream with striking stylised geometric imagery. Materials are polished walnut and beech veneer, chrome-plated metal, cream enamel, bakelite and enamelled badge plates with raised edges. Forms are rounded, generous and warmly glossy, with a firm heavy presence and crisp mid-century typography, confident and industrial.'),
('Grundig','Europe','1950s-present','electronics','In the style of Grundig, dependable postwar German craftsmanship. A heraldic crest emblem with a small crown above a shield holding a three-leaf clover shape in black and white, beside a wide, rounded, bold uppercase wordmark in orange, red or deep blue. Palette is walnut brown, cream, soft gold, hammered grey-green, black and bright orange. Materials are figured wood veneer, brushed gold and chrome metal trim, enamelled badge plates, cream and brown plastic and fine woven fabric. Forms are plain, solid, gently curved and carefully proportioned with neat embossed lettering, reliable, modest and long-lasting in character.'),
]
